SOAPBOX: 10 and 15 not as good as last year. 20 and 40 were the bread and
SOAPBOX: butter bands. Conditions seemed soft. I felt weaker than usual.
SOAPBOX: I gave repeats to almost all DX worked on all bands. Saturday
SOAPBOX: night on 40m was rough with noise from pop up storms all over
SOAPBOX: the southern U.S. I have a feeling log check error rate may be
SOAPBOX: an all time high score! My raw score beat last years raw score.
SOAPBOX: Now lets see if I can hang on at log checking and stay ahead last
SOAPBOX: years final score! I could only operate Friday night and Saturday.
SOAPBOX: Family commitments on Sunday. 73, Gene N9TF
SOAPBOX: K3S 100 watts to 6BTV ground mounted with 32 radials, NO TB,
SOAPBOX: just one aluminum pole in the ground with traps!
